    "canonical_url": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/pregnancy/labor-and-delivery/water-breaking-stories",
    "source_record_id": "raw_html_a07202848552be21",
    "udare_article_path": "C:\\Users\\HP\\Documents\\LinkCraftor\\backend\\server\\data\\udare_store\\ws_whattoexpect_com\\articles\\pregnancy-labor-and-delivery-water-breaking-stories_a0720284.html",
    "udare_article_sha256": "ee78aa4adb4762c5e3bf2d0c83117456eb9d7a7b3e9966406a520fb99eaa0c14"
  },
  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/pregnancy/labor-and-delivery/water-breaking-stories",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 35,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you think you peed your pants, think again.",
        "text_sha256": "d7dfa6218d9af7d1d96d0b8edeb06d0c2f6a01499f3141a8fe1681e86a9f881b",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You've probably seen that cliché movie scene: the pregnant woman is leading a corporate board meeting in heels when her water breaks, or maybe she's mid-fight with her partner and boom — she's soaking. If you've never given birth, the act of \"the water breaking\" seems like a cinematic moment in the labor and delivery process. Sorry to break it to you, but it's not always so dramatic.",
        "text_sha256": "c1f3fa99322ba6a84e49a50248b302493e8aa100fd0d60d5d466b10875f3ee58",
        "word_count": 68
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "When your \"water breaks,\" it's actually the amniotic sac rupturing, and it usually happens at the beginning of labor. Often, the doctor does when you're at the hospital , numb on an epidural , and you don't even feel it (at least, that's what happened to me, twice).",
        "text_sha256": "ae2a2ea5c8d21b1d5853a6c7cc6fe8b327411dc50c53758881c778a5759ddba8",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Still, there are some cases when someone's water breaks unexpectedly, making a perfect story that will be told time and again. I recall a friend's water breaking after our prenatal yoga class , and she walked around New York City for hours before realizing it. She described it as a subtle wetness (which if you've been pregnant, you know happens).",
        "text_sha256": "8dbb7a45d810159a8dc678585f99f52e77c96344ca65303a5d7c42065b76ba47",
        "word_count": 60
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you're wondering what it might feel like and when it might happen, get a sneak peek from the moms in the What to Expect Community . Here's what they were doing when their water broke, but be warned: The old wives' tale about sex inducing labor may have some substance to it.",
        "text_sha256": "2ea123665b58a617c31f27000bf18d68e386c096d4fda1dd5dc1d9b266990b44",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "LOLing",
        "text_sha256": "32bdf74a54e18d86292c2f9ad2b01cc99d7f297aa0ca7f0ca094a77e2be69b76",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I was sitting and laughed at a joke! I confirmed it when I went to pee, and a lot more came out, including the mucus plug . Then, I started filling pads up. I was 39 weeks plus four days and that day I had intercourse, went to dinner, and also walked a lot. So who knows what caused it?\" — @Yo44",
        "text_sha256": "a7f8a1057ed604f41ba39d1360a8461065d36e82c9c2cc5fccf71de15bc7ae9a",
        "word_count": 62
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I was watching TV and laughed at a joke. It felt like I just peed myself, and it was, in fact, leaking water. I was doing absolutely nothing to move things along faster because I wanted an October baby [and it was still September] — she had other plans.\" — @jmp1024",
        "text_sha256": "358827c0927c6a96b4192482cea0d46c614ed3065602b0a5f5519b2568e73c4d",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Taking a leak",
        "text_sha256": "4adaafbf439f6d9d7854b4564743c8fd48466213b251ef31b6a6c8945ebcfc0b",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Peeing, lol … it just kept coming. When I stood to walk away, I couldn't make it stop. You can stop urine midstream, but you cannot stop amniotic fluid.\" — @5-peaseinapod",
        "text_sha256": "962090ad9ab1aa9ce1236d416240b024ef68060da00359384c808bc926a3a2d1",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Going pee. I thought, Wow, I sure am peeing a lot — I thought I'd be done by now. Then I realized that what was coming out was definitely not coming from my urethra. — @n-elizabeth22",
        "text_sha256": "d191583d6fe52c6b3cb85d09f19e953495e941a4463e63dd84414fbf46bf9207",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I had gotten up to make breakfast, went pee as usual, went to the kitchen to make something, and something told me to go back to the bathroom. When I sat down, it immediately broke. — @mariaguidi",
        "text_sha256": "4c714a41a43e685d7e91105f87ff5398a56e5081955b7fc5f3ed08b093946ff5",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I sat down on the toilet and had some fluid leak out. I wasn't 100% sure if it was my water breaking. Then I was walking down the stairs to leave the house and had a gush of fluid that soaked through my pants.\" — @grace7087",
        "text_sha256": "f5b3f035cd792521c1475c3b5277916fbf1034961416a672f3e6bbd059788bd1",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Getting beauty rest",
        "text_sha256": "dffbae32cd9d0936a0ebab8c4321a54bf987f8ab48c4c311ee7198d48d8f45ae",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I woke up, felt a pop, and got up to go pee since I was awake anyway. As soon as I stood up it hit the ground like a movie scene. It woke my husband up.\" – @xhx",
        "text_sha256": "92db96e1dd4b3b6af940b7150cf662706645f576e468364d2d53d13972dc3a0c",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Sleeping! I randomly woke up at 1 a.m. and thought, why am I up?! Within a minute, I felt and heard a pop and a gush.\" — @jccc2024",
        "text_sha256": "ac00b673d9cfcfe0e6dfc9f466417832b7305367b9095605fb79eb671356ceb8",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I stood up from the couch. That's it … I had been napping.\" — @almared",
        "text_sha256": "4c85aa9231fdea4f85081fce6fc84bedbe2721ce51261254c7ab1727b18d91e6",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "After sex",
        "text_sha256": "3a2aec86f4c9680f62287dcbe3e70c6ec3699d76a46a4c257e83bbc2a6833c30",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I used my vibrator the night before with nipple stimulation, too, and it broke getting out of bed the next morning. Hubby was at a 24-hour work shift. Sorry, hubs!\" — @pflowers87",
        "text_sha256": "241bc964083e656f68cacfe73147bcd9b95d69dc84b1ac1f7e0e9ce24d6735c0",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I was 38 weeks plus 6 days. I had sex in the morning, went for a long walk in the afternoon, and was on my exercise ball at around 10 p.m. watching The Beach with Leonardo DiCaprio. As I was bouncing, I felt a gush of liquid. I ran to the bathroom and the mucus plug came out.\" — @sapphiresky88",
        "text_sha256": "d37186e882b940c0eb6cf9544c3d19158ec9908df8e94a94ab56a57ede83cd3b",
        "word_count": 60
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "In the bath",
        "text_sha256": "4cf2fa5f94dd964219b2fe150fb425b6555a334aa330fd50bc4bc7d699290d27",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Taking a bath! It broke while I was relaxing in the bath, and I didn't feel anything! Went to bed afterward and woke up in transition three hours later. I got to the hospital and they asked, 'When did your water break?' I said, 'It didn't!' And they said, 'It definitely did — you have no bag of water.' So we can only assume that it all came out in the bath that night, and I never felt a thing!\" — @rmw92",
        "text_sha256": "818e2d607eed83bfab8ffaa2e4ee872d27286b308d9245b595f63d65e9fb43df",
        "word_count": 82
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I was already in labor, so I took a bath to help with the pain. It must have broken while I was in there because when I got to the hospital, they told me it had broken — which was news to me.\" — @samd2112",
        "text_sha256": "66e78392319ac199cd7d1f5ef7020928c2fc7523ecbd4cafdbcea2402c0dd6e1",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "In motion",
        "text_sha256": "e04c5de8969dcb339cf48288854267749b1805fa07f8fcd479fc302c8bb2fcac",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"With my first, I was doing laundry. I am 40 weeks plus one day today, and I'm just waiting for it to happen again.\" — @GabbyGonzalez2021",
        "text_sha256": "db961ecc32b0cc090b0e724dc607d2f2a32b0f368fe1eeb6b916572ebb94becb",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"It broke three weeks early while I was dancing in the kitchen with my toddler. I picked him up, put him on my belly to dance and felt the trickle. At first, I wasn't sure if I peed or it was my water breaking, but when it didn't stop trickling, I knew it was my water.\" — @mountainmama232",
        "text_sha256": "d2ed411bc8d108cfde02a11280642b9563f13d7db63120ef0644ff2b251c0770",
        "word_count": 58
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "While brushing",
        "text_sha256": "b257b18e2fab470edc51dab6bb06718860f537474eb1578d3cf983211248f2a3",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I was brushing my teeth right after getting out of bed. There was a very small leak. I wasn't even sure if it was my water or not, but it was confirmed later that morning at the doctor's office.\" — @mat95",
        "text_sha256": "27afdf2fbb267ce0b72cff7bde0d11e26fb69d3126e302f7affda7d6bd31e23d",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "During active labor",
        "text_sha256": "58ea19a2fad255474b77524ba100669867b96ed50d689750ba5de454180d9804",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"With my second [baby], I was pushing him out, and my water broke as I delivered his head.\" — @Vetmama",
        "text_sha256": "03a9d618cefc047a2a22a7a0ac008bab8d1504143af509dec4db3b08dc437269",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I was in active labor. I felt the urge to push with my contraction when I was 10 [centimeters dilated], so I did and broke my water.\" — @KatieK-2-27",
        "text_sha256": "91d428afee2461f2782de642070061b068fac6a3d23f005768bac5779db2bea6",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"With my second [baby,] the amniotic sac didn't break until minutes before she was born — she was nearly born in the sac! That sac was strong. It broke during a crazy contraction when I was pushing. We'll see what happens this time around.\" — @AndreaS040321",
        "text_sha256": "645374cb32f0d6fd0f0a9b051a1c78f33c77926a335545fcc83552a04460b3e9",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "At an OB-GYN appointment",
        "text_sha256": "8f303795ff066aab4bdadae29764198b25f8c7c9d92c146db84d46f6ab7ecf7c",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"With my first, I went into my 38-week appointment, had a cervical check, and as the doctor was taking out his hand, I felt a gush of water come out. He goes, 'Wait, what was that?' He checked again and was like, 'Okay, get ready to go to the hospital we're having a baby!'\" — @mayfago",
        "text_sha256": "d1586b293f7fa170298cc071a10435add8541d0bf29a782d32001302c4cad30b",
        "word_count": 56
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "blockquote",
        "tag": "blockquote",
        "text": "What to Expect When You're Expecting , 5th edition, Heidi Murkoff. WhatToExpect.com, What to Do If Your Water Breaks During Pregnancy , March 2023. WhatToExpect.com, 15 Moms on What Labor Really Feels Like , October 2024. WhatToExpect.com, Can Sex During Pregnancy Induce Labor? , July 2022.",
        "text_sha256": "071460ed0f297970b5594b5c99ff9d97eb33fc068d01895725f4d076aaf0401e",
        "word_count": 46
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 1146,
    "heading_count": 9
  },
  "title": "FYI: Your Water Can Break While You're Peeing ... or Sleeping",
